I go to a small shop.
It is a kirana shop.
An older shopkeeper is there.
I say, "Namaste."
The shopkeeper smiles and greets me.
There is a list in my hand.
I read the list.
I speak to the shopkeeper.
"I want turmeric."
"I want cumin."
"I also want salt."
The shopkeeper brings those items.
"Do you want anything else?" he asks.
I say, "No, this is enough."
I give fifty rupees.
The shopkeeper gives me those packets.
I put them in my bag.
I like this small shop.
